{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791434780,"nonce":"jCJDsvmqkdG9CL1Xph6bUr0WUOQ=","title":"Class literal arguments do not bind Class\u003cT\u003e type parameters","message":"Native Haxe infers ConstructedRecord for Type.createInstance(ConstructedRecord,[17]) and Type.createEmptyInstance(ConstructedRecord). On 675d1450aafb100a559818e8cda3e8328b939d4b the corresponding macro Context.typeof probe fails its constructor return type check. Losing T sends subsequent method access through Dynamic dispatch rather than the class declaration.\n\nClass.hx declares the core abstract Class\u003cT\u003e. A class literal's TAST expression carries its instance type. Generic argument unification currently compares Class\u003cT\u003e directly to that instance type, so it cannot bind T. Calls whose argument is already a Class\u003cT\u003e variable use ordinary generic unification and should retain that path.\n\nClassValueInference.hx covers direct reflective construction, a user-defined construct\u003cT\u003e(type:Class\u003cT\u003e,value:Int):T wrapper, createEmptyInstance typing, class instance methods and identity, and a stored Class\u003cConstructedRecord\u003e variable. It passes native Haxe. Prototype v1 binds the Class\u003cT\u003e parameter from literal type values while preserving ordinary instance arguments and typed class variables. Release and corpus gates are pending.\n\nArtifacts: /tmp/rayzor-reflection-construction-native-v1.log, /tmp/rayzor-reflection-construction-before-v1.log, /tmp/rayzor-class-values-native-v1.log.","files":null}]}